# notebook

## Chapter 1

you need to start small and work your way up to advance areas, **metaprograming** is about manupulating and inspecting the ast

```elixir
quote do: div(10,2)
```

macros recieves ast and returns ast (abstrac syntax tree)

```elixir
quote do: 1*3+3
```

```elixir
defmodule Math do
  defmacro say({:+, _, [lhs, rhs]}) do
    quote do
      lhs = unquote(lhs)
      rhs = unquote(rhs)
      result = lhs + rhs
      IO.puts "#{lhs} plus #{rhs} == #{result}"
      result
    end 
  end

  defmacro say({:*, _, [lhs, rhs]}) do
    quote do
      lhs = unquote(lhs)
      rhs = unquote(rhs)
      result = lhs * rhs
      IO.puts "#{lhs} times #{rhs} == #{result}"
      result
    end
  end
end
```

```elixir
require Math
Math.say 5+3
Math.say 5*3*3 + 9
quote do: Math.say 5*3


```

